    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1193">

                <pb facs="1200" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg914"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1193-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-21T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2760. American Red Cross desires to ship relief supplies for Serbia from United
                    States to Holland, thence by land to Serbia. Ascertain attitude of British
                    Government relative to such shipments, taking care to word your inquiries so as
                    not to admit expressly or by implication any right of Great Britain to interfere
                    with such shipments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1193-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d1193-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ambassador in
                    France, No. 1331.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
